body:

Labbonet is a chat client and workflow orchestrator for inference services
that you already run. It is not an engine installer: it connects to local or
trusted-network providers such as Strata and LM Studio, treats them as
interchangeable, and records which model actually produced each reply so a
conversation can move between models without losing its history.

The application is a small Go backend with a browser interface. The backend
holds credentials, talks only to endpoints you have registered, and stores
conversations in SQLite. It listens on the loopback interface by default, asks
for no elevated privileges, changes no firewall or antivirus settings, and
downloads no executables. Its extension surface is declarative, so macros and
appearance presets are validated values rather than scripts or stylesheets.

Labbonet's functional and visual reference is GobboNet by Elodine / GoblinCorps.
The project reuses selected pinned presentation source under AGPLv3-or-later and
documents each reused element, separating copied source, adapted behavior, and
Labbonet's own implementation. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by
GobboNet or its authors.

## Where it stands

Version V0-2-0 is in development. The Phase 1 foundation and the GobboNet
parity milestones for characters, card import and export, branching threads,
detached generation, lore retrieval, optional web search, macros, and schedules
are implemented, and the owner has passed visual approval for the current
interface. Verification against real embedding, search, and summarizer services
is deferred. Provider authentication and cold-start checks, together with final
Phase 1 sign-off, are deferred until V2-0-0. Those items are open, not passed.
